[{:db/id "q-66012/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4412eb27-8cc3-5e2e-a7a2-c161c6ef2ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0709cf0d-44ce-57f0-bd22-3f56c2bde43d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9e329fae-76c1-567f-a977-1cf3bb3a985d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "1335c7b4-c666-572b-adc8-e0aa103ccd53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f11aef9c-4d45-5c24-b2d6-d054fa6edbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "293d9783-5238-5551-9dc6-6fa13b640c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-66012/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-66012/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-66012/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-66012/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-66012/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66012" :question/id #uuid "fe19d5a7-c609-58e7-8ed1-cb1a6db89bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-66012" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=1$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=5$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-66012/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66012"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection/1d1e1445afc3d9a1828e05ecd03637d58e146a26b090f2143764290c35759336" :answer/id #uuid "ea39e055-5de4-585f-97ed-39e723985c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection/2cb480d9a9851c91c435bbf82cedd4c11933f683c1bce4e019ea5a5030b4cee1" :answer/id #uuid "18c72fd7-7074-5ae2-9400-b44091936f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection/908d1d9015b4446f7f4613238506c21dfacedd5aec03544c694256ff366be30b" :answer/id #uuid "27318a66-d3e2-5621-8781-bbe4df52f384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection/246b1ad58cc0969c77bd997655beb7d4737ff4d12f57a35d53e14fdf478570e8" :answer/id #uuid "f90118d7-f44b-59be-bf1f-2d7b079983d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection/65cca031fb0c3d58e669bcbabbe43f8d54e4350ed6e256d1f00fa76238fc83d6" :answer/id #uuid "64c8e833-cba1-5130-8af1-abf68cf117a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e094223-59b6-58d3-90b2-590de6868b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76490/selection/908d1d9015b4446f7f4613238506c21dfacedd5aec03544c694256ff366be30b" :answer-field/choices ["q-76490/selection/1d1e1445afc3d9a1828e05ecd03637d58e146a26b090f2143764290c35759336" "q-76490/selection/2cb480d9a9851c91c435bbf82cedd4c11933f683c1bce4e019ea5a5030b4cee1" "q-76490/selection/908d1d9015b4446f7f4613238506c21dfacedd5aec03544c694256ff366be30b" "q-76490/selection/246b1ad58cc0969c77bd997655beb7d4737ff4d12f57a35d53e14fdf478570e8" "q-76490/selection/65cca031fb0c3d58e669bcbabbe43f8d54e4350ed6e256d1f00fa76238fc83d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76490" :question/id #uuid "7e4cf6db-dd8e-5ff4-9ab3-5bd762661521" :question/math-academy-id "q-76490" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=6$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{6})=1.403\\,348…≈1.403\\,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.403\\,3$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.403\\,3.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=1.403\\,3.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=1.403\\,3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041448/assets/9b3d60be42ec916f0e62f3a86cb1ce2aa628482c97f68f0df7c6ab533b919102.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =2\\pi -1.403\\,3 \\\\  & ≈4.879\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.403\\,3\\,\\cdot 4.879\\,9≈6.8\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76490/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387e57ad-6f80-5b90-8adf-7bf05618b532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection/15c9994fd4827b5d6f911b13d40a31e2e1b39a703ed8fecba24f8133ecdcc9fa" :answer/id #uuid "ca25e273-1120-52a0-9763-1d7b602fc5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{35{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection/d2b5410439250a48dfc47a30937d12717d16f3ac6857e8147eb7f5c2a35f07e3" :answer/id #uuid "cdceaee8-a8b2-5f5a-835e-a6293fb0ce56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection/d17929b524c9f857430aad13d2b82b399e0428d115c048255e3eec906c48b8fd" :answer/id #uuid "83fca5ad-19a5-527a-9bb9-37b38211147f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{35{\\pi }^{2}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection/1469cb3234d8827d90ce635fea976fd9f8898ec812577cad4fcea5557d011275" :answer/id #uuid "2a74faa0-7119-5997-841d-9b5618bdc696" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection/8d54d5a33a4a6335cbac07172f6ca8a7c8d5747aa3e69924290a2799a513ba90" :answer/id #uuid "a189b7c2-33ae-56d1-90db-59a2427e71bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae8ea27e-a9c0-5393-a13c-254b828bd181" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76499/selection/15c9994fd4827b5d6f911b13d40a31e2e1b39a703ed8fecba24f8133ecdcc9fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-76499/selection/15c9994fd4827b5d6f911b13d40a31e2e1b39a703ed8fecba24f8133ecdcc9fa" "q-76499/selection/d2b5410439250a48dfc47a30937d12717d16f3ac6857e8147eb7f5c2a35f07e3" "q-76499/selection/d17929b524c9f857430aad13d2b82b399e0428d115c048255e3eec906c48b8fd" "q-76499/selection/1469cb3234d8827d90ce635fea976fd9f8898ec812577cad4fcea5557d011275" "q-76499/selection/8d54d5a33a4a6335cbac07172f6ca8a7c8d5747aa3e69924290a2799a513ba90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76499" :question/id #uuid "4e8521fd-ad2a-559c-8610-d33a7fbf2c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-76499" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $-2\\pi <x<0,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ is not in the domain $-2\\pi <x<0.$ To get the first solution within the required domain, we subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041448/assets/afb20de50d2fa92c6550d1e5357b2aaf07311177e3ed82e1a15facccf2c0f0db.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value does not lie in the required domain. To get the solution that's within the given domain, we subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{6},-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=\\frac{35{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76499/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28062dbf-815b-5221-ae86-1050e106c5ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76499"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396/field-1/811360346a398c62c03c5a0e34ed720c82397841ac791e2c2d8ef5cf09ac86dd" :answer/id #uuid "b10494cc-d252-5978-b1a4-db1487a0a91b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "78.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396/field-1/3e8ef1b15241197f446155c82fa01b67a9c82ede3395f43045f100219fe2f25c" :answer/id #uuid "1881eefe-e262-5134-8f39-9602f168ac73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "78.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "26f0f00d-12e5-5e5c-af9a-a051137faf9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324396/field-1/811360346a398c62c03c5a0e34ed720c82397841ac791e2c2d8ef5cf09ac86dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-324396/field-1/811360346a398c62c03c5a0e34ed720c82397841ac791e2c2d8ef5cf09ac86dd" "q-324396/field-1/3e8ef1b15241197f446155c82fa01b67a9c82ede3395f43045f100219fe2f25c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396/field-2/2d134fe77d3870d7d766e5a8d302eb097202b05604cbcc70b94b02de273d1885" :answer/id #uuid "c0897369-ac95-5e88-8e19-1efce92a255e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "281.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e70b34da-e74d-5abc-9184-813d0d76b95a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324396/field-2/2d134fe77d3870d7d766e5a8d302eb097202b05604cbcc70b94b02de273d1885" :answer-field/choices ["q-324396/field-2/2d134fe77d3870d7d766e5a8d302eb097202b05604cbcc70b94b02de273d1885"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324396" :question/id #uuid "e0811f8e-77b1-581c-9a3b-49215eb91c06" :question/math-academy-id "q-324396" :question/problem "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=5$ for $0\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value of $x,$ rounded to three decimal places:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arccos\\,(\\frac{1}{5})≈{78.463}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}≈{78.463}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the $4$th quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}≈{78.463}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041448/assets/e05c5b50dc8308d278cb6dac3408349da1865d37601003e0ee3025c937404239.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ≈{360}^{∘}-{78.463}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{281.537}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=78.5\\,{\\,}^{∘}$\nand $x=281.5\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-324396/field-1" "q-324396/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387e57ad-6f80-5b90-8adf-7bf05618b532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-324396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325113/field-1/c3c6c459ed4a41e1787e73fcd54c86c54db8639b1d960afc80ba4dad429691c3" :answer/id #uuid "7ade66cd-d4ea-52b3-8c97-f074b46d9065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325113/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0006b45-c61a-57d2-bd9d-6f06140121b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325113/field-1/c3c6c459ed4a41e1787e73fcd54c86c54db8639b1d960afc80ba4dad429691c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-325113/field-1/c3c6c459ed4a41e1787e73fcd54c86c54db8639b1d960afc80ba4dad429691c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325113/field-2/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "eda27441-a598-55a1-98e8-d0f8dd842437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325113/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e8ee893-56a2-5891-b9a4-7a32d4796e8e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325113/field-2/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer-field/choices ["q-325113/field-2/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325113" :question/id #uuid "f0b4a712-747b-5f24-a07c-8792364dfb5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-325113" :question/problem "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-2$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x<{180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arccos\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})={120}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $x={120}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={120}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={180}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}={60}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={60}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041448/assets/29560b074afbb7d4e0cde3c1964e14696ef9879618e42c0b0c41f478e7ffcb72.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the third quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={240}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={240}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-120\\,{\\,}^{∘}$ and $x=120\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325113/field-1" "q-325113/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28062dbf-815b-5221-ae86-1050e106c5ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
